{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794757475,"nonce":"hRazXu0jK6eydF9LxDe9J32GHBU=","title":"wasm fibers: a call to a library native made its whole function untransformable, so a thread that slept inside one trapped","message":"Seen by hxn: a Haxe thread that calls into a side-module library and sleeps trapped with `wasm unreachable` under ASH_WASM_FIBERS=1 (exit 70, every run) and passed without fibers. The generated fixture, whose threads do not call library natives from a function that also suspends, passed.\n\nCause. `call_native_slot` (ash_wasm_emit/src/calls.rs) pushed the call's arguments, then loaded the native's slot and tested it inside an `if` whose body calls `hlp_aot_native_missing`. That call is in the suspend set, and the fiber transform cannot spill operands that were pushed before the control frame it is in, so it refused the whole function. A refused function that can be on the stack at a suspend gets a guard that traps when the state is unwinding, and that is the `unreachable`. The same check in wasm_program/links.rs already ran before the arguments.\n\nEvidence, from the module hxn left behind. In the printed text of main.wasm, Fun_438 (calls hlp_sys_sleep and three library natives) has 12 guards that are all a plain `unreachable`; 1998 other functions have guard bodies that spill and unwind; 65 have only plain guards. `ASH_FIBER_REPORT=1` on the rebuild prints `instrumented 1998 function(s), refused 65 (0 holding an unsavable value)`. The same shape appears in every function that calls a library native through a slot.\n\nFix: check the slot before pushing the arguments. The arguments are plain local reads, so the order is not observable.\n\nLeft to do:\n- The refusal count is printed only with ASH_FIBER_REPORT, so a build with refusals looks clean. Print one line whenever refused is not zero.\n- Nothing checks the emitted shape. A test that runs the fiber transform over a body with a native-slot call and requires `refused == 0` would have caught this.\n- The next shape that puts a suspending call inside a frame over live operands will do the same thing; the emitter has no rule against it.","files":null}]}